00:58:50,769 --> 00:58:56,769
Winterland, called at first New Dreamland Auditorium and later Winterland Arena and Winterland Ballroom, was an
ice-skating rink and music venue in San Francisco operational from 1928 to 1979 and demolished in 1986.

10
01:05:23,076 --> 01:05:29,076
Built at the corner of Post Street and Steiner Street, it was converted for exclusive use for music
in 1971 by concert promoter Bill Graham, who made it a popular stop for rock acts.

11
01:11:55,384 --> 01:12:01,384
Graham's related merchandising company Winterland Productions sold
concert shirts, memorabilia and sports-team merchandise.

12
01:18:27,692 --> 01:18:33,692
The tone is emotional.
